title The card that narrated itself
prompt Autonomous loop -- condense the done work out of ITINERARY and refill its Now with live work so the card stays single-stranded
think The card's Git nib stood four rounds stale at `7f268a25fd`, and `remember-git-nib.md` refuses a pin-only follow-up commit. So the pin needed real work to ride with, and the card's own front-doors table already named that work: ITINERARY at 76,439 bytes, over the 24,576 pin bound, wanting condensation on touch.
think Measured the sections before cutting. `## INNER LOOP` held **50,477 bytes** -- 65% of the whole card -- and its own heading says *live directives the running loop applies each lap*, with its own instruction to move settled items down into the body.
obs Of its 22 bullets, five are directives and fifteen are landed-round narratives with stamps from `20260817` to `20260823`. Below the bullets sat a stack of `Now --`, `Prior lap --` and `Elder note --` blocks describing rounds that had closed days earlier. That is the second copy of the log index the card's own habits section forbids.
think Kept what is live and cut what is recorded. Live: the five standing directives, the seated names and breaches, the banked deep-debride grant, the Caravan semi-standfast, the host line, and the four `20260815` crypto-spine decisions. Everything else reads as one line in Prior laps or Landed arcs, pointing at the log holding its detail.
obs Added two directives the block was missing and the loop actually runs: roster cold then hot after `git add` (REDS %174), and reds first. A directive the loop follows and the card omits is the same drift in the other direction.
obs Checkpoint `7754ccf272` first, since the departing body holds fifteen round narratives written at the time -- their numbers, their checkpoints, their reds. Each also has its own session log; the walk-back is the fastest way to read them as one arc.
loom card=construction/ITINERARY.md bytes_before=77588 bytes_after=41449 inner_loop_before=50477 inner_loop_after=14092
file construction/ITINERARY.md the INNER LOOP block condensed to directives; the Git nib names `7754ccf272` and this lap's rounds; the front-doors table and Prior laps updated
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md walk-back row at `7754ccf272` naming what waits in the departing block
recommend keep-going `caravan/README.md` at 497,531 bytes over 2,694 lines is the Tier 1 crux the ranked remainder names -- a Door page for the tree's largest module, with the 110-rung ladder table lifted to its own reference page
